# Cloudflare Pages security headers (Doctrine §16.6).
#
# These cost one file and break nothing. A Content-Security-Policy is worth more
# and costs more — it is a refactor rather than a header anywhere a page carries
# inline script — so what is here is stated honestly rather than implied:
# MoleBridge has NO Content-Security-Policy yet. It has no inline script either,
# so one is reachable; it is owed, and it is not here.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()

# The worker must never be served from a cache older than itself, or a new
# release cannot arrive at all.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/precache.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
